{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Solving Problems", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Let's Go to the Lunchroom ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "Beginner", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Ask for Permission", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you ask for permission, you ask to do something or have something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Alex</span>:  Can I have a cookie, please?<br/> <span class = \"strong\">Betty</span>: Sure you can.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> can </span> or <span class=\"strong\"> could </span> to ask for permission. <span class=\"strong\"> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Alice</span>: Could I ask you some questions?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Bob</span>: Not now, I'm busy.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Say No in a Polite Way ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to say no in a polite way. you use expressions like \"I'm a little busy\", \"Sorry, not now\" or \"That's okay. Thanks.\"", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Carol</span>: Can you help me with my homework? <br/><span class = \"strong\">Tim</span>: I'm sorry. I'm a little busy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Joan</span>: Can I help you with that?<br/> <span class = \"strong\">Mike</span> : That's okay. Thanks.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Where can I find ... ?", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ask about the location of a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Where can I find a good restaurant?", "type